Original commit body from aac78ff5a03b01a56c6151c02e55c328ed5540be:

The module-attr / variable-ref retarget resolves `cfg.CONFIG` to a real
first-party symbol when `cfg` is an in-tree module alias, guarded by a
shadow set so a local that rebinds the alias stays phantom. That set was
built from ast.Name/ast.Store assignment targets only -- but four forms
bind a name WITHOUT one:

  - a module-level `def cfg` / `class cfg` (the statement binds in the
    enclosing scope, even though its body opens a new one)
  - `except E as cfg` (ExceptHandler.name is a bare str, not a Name node)
  - a walrus `(cfg := ...)` inside a comprehension, which per PEP 572
    binds in the CONTAINING scope
  - the same def/class collision one scope out, where a nested function's
    read closes over an enclosing statement name

Each left a confidently-wrong RESOLVED edge pointing at the module's real
symbol -- the INV-fahub failure class -- and each was documented in-code
as an accepted residual, with the fix shape named ("a dedicated
per-function shadow collector distinct from the LEGB local_names set").

All four reproduced on a live probe before any code changed; the fix is
_collect_statement_binding_names, unioned into the module-scope rebind
walk and into _enclosing_shadow via a per-function map built inside
_extract_edges (which already has the tree and the node->symbol map, so
no FileAnalysis field is threaded).

Kept deliberately SEPARATE from _collect_scope_local_names: that set
feeds the LEGB lookup, which resolves def/class names to their NestedDef
bindings directly and would break if they were treated as opaque locals.
This one is a shadow set, not a lookup set.

Safety: every name it adds can only turn a retarget resolved -> phantom
(a missed retarget), never phantom -> resolved. A non-vacuous control
test asserts an UNSHADOWED alias still retargets to the real CONFIG
variable, so the shadow cannot silently over-approximate.

Note for future readers: the first draft of these tests asserted "no edge
anywhere targets CONFIG" and failed on the containment linker's entirely
correct `contains` file->variable edge. The assertion must be scoped to
the retarget edge types AND to the reading file.

